---
import Layout from "../../layouts/Layout.astro";
import ExamShell from "../../components/ExamShell.astro";
import ExamPractice from "../../components/ExamPractice.astro";
---
<Layout
  title="IELTS Academic: format, band scores and practice – icanspeak Spanish"
  description="IELTS Academic: the English test many universities ask for — how it works, how band scores work, and practice."
>
  <ExamShell
    bild="testdaf"
    header="IELTS Academic"
    title="IELTS Academic"
    lead="The English test many universities ask for. It reports band scores from 0 to 9 and has no pass mark."
    leadKey="testdaf.lead"
    badges={["Bands 0–9"]}
    practiceHeading="Practise for IELTS"
    practiceHeadingKey="testdaf.practiceHeading"
  >
    <Fragment slot="info">
      <section class="exam-section">
        <h2 data-i18n="testdaf.who.title">Who is IELTS Academic for?</h2>
        <div class="exam-meta-row">
          <span class="exam-meta-badge" data-i18n="testdaf.who.badge.result">Result: band scores 0–9</span>
          <span class="exam-meta-badge" data-i18n="testdaf.who.badge.oneFormat">One format for everyone</span>
        </div>
        <p data-i18n="testdaf.who.text">
          IELTS Academic is aimed mainly at people applying to universities and colleges that teach in
          English. Everyone sits the same four parts (Listening, Reading, Writing and Speaking). Each
          skill gets a band score from 0 to 9, and you also get an overall band. There is no pass mark:
          every institution decides which bands it asks for, so check the requirement of your course.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="exam-section">
        <h2 data-i18n="exam.skills.title">Skills tested</h2>
        <div class="skill-grid">
          <div class="skill-card"><div class="skill-card-icon">📖</div><h4 data-i18n="skill.lesen">Reading</h4><p data-i18n="skill.lesen.desc">Reading comprehension</p></div>
          <div class="skill-card"><div class="skill-card-icon">🎧</div><h4 data-i18n="skill.hoeren">Listening</h4><p data-i18n="skill.hoeren.desc">Listening comprehension</p></div>
          <div class="skill-card"><div class="skill-card-icon">✍️</div><h4 data-i18n="skill.schreiben">Writing</h4><p data-i18n="skill.schreiben.desc">Written expression</p></div>
          <div class="skill-card"><div class="skill-card-icon">🗣️</div><h4 data-i18n="skill.sprechen">Speaking</h4><p data-i18n="skill.sprechen.oralDesc">Spoken expression</p></div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="exam-section">
        <!-- GENERIC FORMAT INFO: no icanspeak Spanish source material for this exam yet -->
        <h2 data-i18n="exam.format.title">Format</h2>
        <div class="format-table-wrap">
          <table class="format-table">
            <thead><tr><th data-i18n="format.th.part">Part</th><th data-i18n="format.th.what">What is tested</th><th data-i18n="format.th.duration">Duration (approx.)</th></tr></thead>
            <tbody>
              <tr><td data-i18n="skill.lesen.desc">Reading comprehension</td><td data-i18n="testdaf.fmt.lesen.what">Three long texts with a range of question types</td><td data-i18n="testdaf.fmt.min60">approx. 60 min.</td></tr>
              <tr><td data-i18n="skill.hoeren.desc">Listening comprehension</td><td data-i18n="testdaf.fmt.hoeren.what">Recordings from everyday conversations to an academic talk</td><td data-i18n="testdaf.fmt.min30">approx. 30 min.</td></tr>
              <tr><td data-i18n="skill.schreiben.desc">Written expression</td><td data-i18n="testdaf.fmt.schreiben.what">Task 1: describe a chart, graph, table or diagram. Task 2: an essay giving your view.</td><td data-i18n="testdaf.fmt.min60">approx. 60 min.</td></tr>
              <tr><td data-i18n="skill.sprechen.oralDesc">Spoken expression</td><td data-i18n="testdaf.fmt.sprechen.what">A face-to-face interview with an examiner</td><td data-i18n="testdaf.fmt.min14">approx. 11–14 min.</td></tr>
            </tbody>
          </table>
        </div>
        <p class="format-note" data-i18n="testdaf.format.note">
          There is no pass mark: each skill gets a band score from 0 to 9, you get an overall band, and
          every university or employer decides which bands it asks for. We have no official IELTS
          material of our own; the details here are general, public information about the test. For the
          current format and timings, check the official IELTS website.
        </p>
      </section>
    </Fragment>

    <div class="mock-cta mock-cta--lead">
      <h2 data-i18n="testdaf.set.title">Practise reading in exam style</h2>
      <p data-i18n-html="testdaf.set.text">
        Three reading tasks in the style of IELTS Academic Reading — matching, multiple choice and
        Yes / No / Not given — plus a writing task about a chart, with structure, useful phrases and
        a checklist. All texts and tasks are written by us, not official exam material. Listening is
        still missing — it needs audio recordings.
      </p>
      <a class="quiz-btn quiz-btn--primary" href="/ielts/practice-set" data-i18n="exam.startSet">Start the practice set</a>
    </div>

    <ExamPractice
      heading="Train the basics"
      headingKey="exam.practice.heading"
      intro="Besides the practice set above, these three tools help at every level and for every exam. They test general articles, grammar and vocabulary, not anything IELTS-specific."
      introKey="testdaf.practice.intro"
      tools={["artikel", "grammatik", "wortschatz"]}
    />
  </ExamShell>
</Layout>
